# data/maps/traetoppen.map - TRAETOPPEN, the levelled treetop city (design: DUNGEON_V2_ADDENDUM 7.3, design_v2.md 4; package V4-city-map).
# HEADER ONLY: there is no ground grid. scripts/traetoppen/city_builder.gd (CityBuilder.build(area, header)) builds the whole area from
# data/traetoppen/traetoppen.json (8 platforms, 9 bridges, the ladder, the Skovlift, 14 buildings ...): the levels, the physics bits and the
# draw order are DATA, and a position is walkable when a level holds it (area.walkable_test), which is what a Continue is put back through.
# The @marker lines below are DECLARATIONS for readers and tools (a builder area places no object chars): the arrival spawns and the three
# ways out. The data file owns the numbers (spawns, the two bridge stubs, the lift); the section city_map checks that these lines and the data
# say the same (city_map.header_declarations_match_the_data). `default` (the Torvet, beside the fire pit) is implicit like in every map.
#   from_farm       tree G, east rim        the farm bridge lands here        warp at the end of the farm stub  -> farm:from_traetoppen
#   from_hyggebyen  tree F, west rim        the Hyggebyen bridge lands here   warp at the end of the F stub     -> hyggebyen:from_traetoppen
#   from_skovlift   tree B rim at the rope  the forest hub's gate lands here  the Skovlift (RopeLift, E)        -> moerkeskoven:from_traetoppen
# @zoom_min 0.2 shows the whole composition of the sketch (it fits at 0.237 wide / 0.19 high); the area sizes its own sky and far backdrop.
# The camera may scroll 450 world px above the sketch's top edge (area.bounds, CityBuilder.HEADROOM_PX) so the top platforms A and B are not drawn under the
# canopy frame, and the frame thins out when zoomed out (16 percent of the screen at 0.4, 4 percent at 0.2): the whole composition is visible at the minimum zoom.
# A builder area is never parked: every visit builds again (warm rebuild budget 40 ms; if a real-art rebuild ever exceeds the 0.22 s fade the
# decision is ONE header line `@cache true`, not a code change).
@id traetoppen
@title ZONE_TRAETOPPEN
@projection iso
@ambient farm
@theme treetop
@zone traetoppen
@flight false
@music city_theme
@zoom 0.4
@zoom_min 0.2
@zoom_max 0.7
@builder res://scripts/traetoppen/city_builder.gd
@marker f spawn name=from_farm
@marker h spawn name=from_hyggebyen
@marker s spawn name=from_skovlift
@marker F warp to=farm spawn=from_traetoppen label=ZONE_FARM
@marker H warp to=hyggebyen spawn=from_traetoppen label=ZONE_CITY
@marker S warp to=moerkeskoven spawn=from_traetoppen label=ZONE_FOREST_EDGE
